.Dd August 16, 2026
.Dt CTRLMENU 3
.Os libcontrol
.Sh NAME
.Nm ctrlmenu_popup ,
.Nd pop-up menu routines
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In X11/Xlib.h
.In X11/Xresource.h
.In control/menu.h
.Bd -literal
struct ctrlmenu_entry {
	char *label;
	size_t labellen;

	char *output;
	char *altoutput;
	char *file;

	struct ctrlmenu_entry *children;
	size_t nchildren;
};
.Ed
.Pp
.Ft void
.Fo ctrlmenu_popup
.Fa "Display *display"
.Fa "int screen_number"
.Fa "XrmDatabase resurces"
.Fa "Visual *visual"
.Fa "int depth"
.Fa "Colormap colormap"
.Fa "struct ctrlmenu_entry *entries"
.Fa "size_t nentries"
.Fa "char const *title"
.Fa "Window leader"
.Fa "int x_root"
.Fa "int y_root"
.Fa "Time timestamp"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The ctrlmenu library implements both a pop-up menu
(used as context menu, or start menu, for example),
and a torn-off menu.
.Pp
The
.Fn ctrlmenu_popup
function creates a pop-up menu on an override-redirect window
(i'e', not managed by the window manager)
with the given
.Fa entries .
It blocks as long as the menu is popped up
(i'e', until an entry is selected or the menu is closed).
.Pp
The
.Ft "struct ctrlmenu_entry"
structure specifies one of the entries listed in a menu.
An array of such entries makes a menu.
.Ss Parameters
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fa display , screen_number
The pointer to the context of connection to the
.Xr Xserver 1 ;
and the index of the
.Fa display Ap s
screen.
.It Fa entries , nentries
The array of menu entries that make the menu;
and the number of members in such array.
.It Fa leader
The ID of the client window that the menu is a context of.
If the menu is not a context menu (or transient for a main window),
this argument should be
.Dv None .
.It Fa resources
The resource database with configuration for the menu look and feel.
If
.Dv NULL ,
resource is not processed.
.It Fa timestamp
The time of the event that triggered the menu to pop up.
.It Fa title
The title of the menu
(to be displayed by the window manager if the menu gets windowed/torn-off).
.It Fa visual , depth , colormap
The triplet of graphic information for visual type, color depth, and color map,
needed for Xlib drawing routines.
.It Fa x_root , y_root
The
.Pq Em x,y
position where the menu is popped up.
.El
.Ss Entry structure
The
.Ft ctrlmenu_entry
structure contains the definitions of a menu entry.
Its members are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fa label , labellen
UTF-8 string to be displayed on the entry; and its length.
If
.Dv NULL ,
the entry is a separator.
.It Fa output
String to be printed when the entry is activated.
If
.Dv NULL ,
the entry is inactive
(dimmed and cannot be selected nor activated).
.It Fa altoutput
String to be printed when the entry is activated by alternate means:
with the middle mouse button, or while pressing the
.Em Shift
key.
.It Fa file
TODO
.It Fa children , nchildren
The array of entries of the submenu that is created when the entry is activated;
and the number of members of such array.
If
.Dv NULL ,
the entry does not pops up a submenu.
.El
.Ss Popup function
The
.Fa ctrlmenu_popup
function pops up a menu with the given
.Fa entries ,
and blocks until the menu is closed
(either by activating an entry or closing the menu).
